		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How long does it take to ship a car?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"It takes around 5–7 days to ship a car across the country with the best auto transport companies. It can take anywhere from 1 to 3 days to ship a vehicle with local and nationwide car moving companies. The following auto shipping factors may affect your delivery window: Weather conditions, Equipment issues, Road closures, Location changes, Driver availability, Time of year. When you schedule with Nexus, one of our experts will connect you with a top independent auto transport driver known for professionalism and punctuality. We provide contact details for the trucking and shipping of your car, and they will return your calls as soon as possible. Feel free to contact our experienced transport coordinators at (224) 218-2949 for more information on how long it will take to ship your car, or any other information regarding current and completed auto shipping orders. Auto transporting companies. Car transport company. Vehicle shipping companies. Car transport companies."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How much does it cost to ship a car?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"The cost of shipping a car starts at $299 and averages around $775. Auto shipment prices vary, depending on the day and the auto transporting companies you get quotes from. Factors that affect cost include: Total car shipping distance, The flexibility of your delivery schedule, Vehicle condition (operational or inoperable), Your vehicle make & model, Time of year, Fuel prices, Type of car transport (open, enclosed, expedited), Driver availability, Consumer demand. Nexus works with a vast network of pro car shippers, and each trucker has different pricing demands from route to route and season to season. Nexus Auto Transport has created an accurate, instant auto transport price calculator to simplify pricing and get your transparent quotes at any time of day. Get a free, anonymous vehicle shipping quote within seconds to learn about the costs of your car shipment. So, how much does it cost to ship a car? Visit our private car transport calculator to find out, or call (224) 218-2949 to be connected with a dedicated automotive shipping professional."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How do I find the best car shipping company?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Do your research before choosing between car shipping companies. You have dozens of potential car carriers to choose from, whether you're shipping a car across the country or need to relocate a car a couple of hundred miles. The difference between the best auto transport companies and the others often comes down to transparency, experience, and professionalism. Nexus Auto Transport boasts one of the most experienced and well-trained support staffs in the industry. Rather than vetting private car haulers yourself, let an informed car transport expert pair you with the correct driver for your needs. Our dispatch team organizes everything for you, and we only work with the most reliable professional car haulers on the road. It's all about eliminating worries for you and giving you the security you pay for. All vehicle shipping quotes are accurately assessed and include comprehensive, door-to-door car transport management services."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How do I prepare a car for shipping?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Here's how to plan to ship a car direct with professional car shipping companies: Clean your car inside and out (aids inspections); Take photos of all pre-existing damage (compare notes with carriers); Drop your gas to a quarter tank (reduce weight while ensuring driveability); Remove personal items from your car before shipping (unless otherwise permitted). The cleaner and more prepared your car is for processing by vehicle shipping companies, the easier it will be for our trucking partner to move your car!"
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How safe is professional auto shipping?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Professional auto transporters are usually safer than driving a car yourself from state to state or across the country. Use a top broker like Nexus Auto Transport to connect with the safest drivers in the United States. All vehicle shipping quotes secured via our online auto shipping price calculator or at (224) 218-2949 include secure, safe door-to-door service. We take pride in being a reliable car shipping company, centered on exceptional customer care. Let our knowledgeable car transport coordinators assist you. We've built connections with the safest car movers in the industry, and you get the benefits of those partnerships. Nexus is dedicated to both our customers and the private car haulers we assign. It is our studied, interpersonal approach that helps us maintain our reputation as a safe vehicle transport company."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How do I choose an auto transport company?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Look for vehicle transport companies with credible web presences. The top vehicle shipping companies will be licensed by the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMCSA) and fully accredited by the Better Business Bureau (BBB). Check out reviews on multiple websites and verify any information you find against what the vehicle transport company claims. Nexus Auto Transport provides comprehensive car moving services through carefully selected trucking partners. Our car hauling packages start with accurate automotive quotes secured through our car shipping cost calculator. From there, a dedicated support specialist will manage your vehicle transport from start to finish. We value your time and will ensure that your vehicle receives the utmost care from pickup through delivery. We rank highly in consumer ratings, with a 4.7 rating on TrustPilot. See why media outlets like Forbes and MarketWatch feature us as one of the best auto shipping companies in the nation."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"Can you ship your car with its contents inside?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Most professional transportation companies require you to remove all personal items from your car before it is transported. Nexus Auto Transport understands that special circumstances may arise; please contact us at (224) 218-2949 if you require personalized assistance. We will work diligently to find a car hauler that meets your specific needs."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What Nexus Auto Transport discounts are available?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Nexus Auto Transport offers multi-vehicle shipping discounts, military discounts, senior discounts, back-to-school discounts, and a $500 discount for car dealerships that ship ten cars through our Nexus Dealer Portal. We also offer cash discounts for those paying drivers at delivery. Nexus is willing to work with budgets of all sizes. Please call (224) 218-2949 for 5-star car shipping services."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What types of car shipping does Nexus offer?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Here are the ways you can transport a vehicle through Nexus Auto Transport: Open car shipping: the most popular and cheapest way to ship; door-to-door haulers often carry multiple vehicles—recommended for most vehicles valued under $70,000. Enclosed car transport: a premium, fully sheltered option that helps ward off dust, debris, rocks, weather complications, and potential theft—select it from the scheduling page options. Expedited auto transport: when timing is tight—Nexus prioritizes your order and works to find a driver quickly (windows cannot be guaranteed). Inoperable vehicle transportation: pay an additional fee for specialized service (winch or similar tool) if the car is not drivable—protection is the same as for operating vehicles. Nexus takes a simple approach: direct, door-to-door services and an experienced auto transport team."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How does car transport work?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"The car transport process is as easy as 1, 2, 3 with Nexus Auto Transport: 1) Get your free vehicle shipping quote from our instant vehicle transport costs calculator, or call 224-218-2949 and schedule pickup within minutes online or by phone; 2) Prep your car for shipment—clean inside and out, document pre-existing damage with photos, your driver will contact you 24 hours before pickup and arrange an adjacent spot if your location is inaccessible; 3) A vetted private car hauler delivers your car—final inspection for new damage, sign the BoL, get your keys, and you're done. Nexus provides comprehensive management from start to finish."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What does Nexus Auto Transport specialize in?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Nexus Auto Transport is a knowledgeable car transporting service provider that connects door-to-door car shipping companies for clients across the United States. We specialize in standard open car shipping services, luxury car shipping, military car shipping, enclosed vehicle transportation, motorcycle shipping, and a wide range of other private and commercial vehicle transport options. Nexus is also a dedicated car transport services provider for car dealerships around the nation via the Nexus Dealer Portal. Nexus Auto Transport has received over 5,000 five-star reviews in its ten years of operation. Secure a free quote from our car transportation calculator, or call 224-218-2949 to get started."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What paperwork is required to ship a car?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"The only required paperwork for car transport services is the Bill of Lading (BoL), an official vehicle condition report that records the vehicle's condition, pickup, and delivery details and is signed by the carrier and the customer. You do not need to show your title, insurance, or registration for car relocation service because your vehicle will not be driven during transit."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What is the most reliable car shipping company?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Nexus Auto Transport is one of the most trusted auto transport companies in the United States. With over 500,000 customers and thousands of 5-star reviews, Nexus specializes in affordable car transport. Our door-to-door carrier network is vetted for safety, security, and efficiency."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What types of vehicles can you ship?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Nexus Auto Transport provides nationwide car shipping services for the following vehicles: Standard passenger vehicles, SUVs, Trucks, Luxury car transport, Exotic vehicle shipping, Classic car shipping for vintage and collector cars, Electric vehicle transport (EV shipping), Motorcycle shipping, ATV transport, Inoperable vehicle transport, Heavy equipment and commercial vehicle transport."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"What should I do to prepare my car for transport?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Nexus Auto Transport provides complete auto transport services from scheduling through pickup. To ensure things run smoothly: Clean your car inside and out to aid inspection; Remove all personal items for lower shipping weight; Check fluid levels, tire pressure, and battery; Disable alarms and remove any toll passes; Take photos of all pre-existing damage."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"Does Nexus offer door-to-door auto transport?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Yes! Nexus partners with the nation's top auto haulers to provide door-to-door car shipping to all 50 U.S. states. Your driver is committed to picking up and delivering your vehicle as close as possible to your specified locations."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"Can I track my vehicle during the car transport process?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Yes, Nexus Auto Transport provides a direct communication link with your auto shipping carrier, allowing you to track your car shipment. You can also contact customer support at (224) 218-2949 with questions or concerns."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"How can I order car shipping services with Nexus?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"It's easy to book reliable car transport services with Nexus. To book: Get a free instant car shipping quote using our accurate vehicle transport calculator; Select between open, enclosed, or expedited car shipping; Clean and prepare your vehicle for transport; Stay in touch for email and phone updates on your estimated pickup and delivery times."
		}
		},
		{
		"@type":"Question",
		"name":"Can Nexus Auto Transport handle multiple vehicle shipments?",
		"acceptedAnswer":{
			"@type":"Answer",
			"text":"Yes! Nexus offers affordable car shipping rates for multi-vehicle shipments, whether you're shipping multiple cars for work, pleasure, or both. Contact one of our vehicle transport specialists for more information."
		}
		}
	]
	}
